Date: Sun, 26 Apr 2026 17:08:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] Items 13-15: Coverage, Clustering, Constrained Delaunay

Item 13 - Coverage processing
  GEOSGeometry::coverageUnion()
  GEOSGeometry::coverageIsValid($gapWidth = 0.0)
                returns ['valid' => bool, 'invalid' => GEOSGeometry]
                ('invalid' is always populated; empty for valid coverages)
  GEOSGeometry::coverageSimplifyVW($tolerance, $simplifyBoundary = true)
  GEOSGeometry::coverageClean($params = [])  with 'snap_distance',
                'gap_max_width', 'overlap_strategy' keys
  Constants under both upstream and plan-preferred names:
    GEOS_MERGE_LONGEST_BORDER / GEOS_OVERLAP_MERGE_LONGEST_BORDER
    GEOS_MERGE_MAX_AREA       / GEOS_OVERLAP_MERGE_MAX_AREA
    GEOS_MERGE_MIN_AREA       / GEOS_OVERLAP_MERGE_MIN_AREA
    GEOS_MERGE_MIN_INDEX      / GEOS_OVERLAP_MERGE_MIN_INDEX

Item 14 - Clustering
  GEOSGeometry::clusterDBSCAN($eps, $minPoints)
  GEOSGeometry::clusterByDistance($distance, $useEnvelope = false)
  GEOSGeometry::clusterByIntersection($useEnvelope = false)

  New class GEOSClusterResult:
    getNumClusters(), getClusterSize($i),
    getClustersForInputs(), getInputsForCluster($n)
  __construct is locked (only via GEOSGeometry::cluster*).

  Implementation note: ClusterRelay struct holds both the C
  GEOSClusterInfo* and the source-collection input count (captured
  at cluster-call time), since upstream omits a getNumElements
  accessor. Dtor frees both.

Item 15 - Constrained Delaunay
  delaunayTriangulation($tolerance = 0, $edgeOnly = false, $constrained = false)
  Optional third arg routes to GEOSConstrainedDelaunayTriangulation_r.

21/21 .phpt tests pass.
